Day 12: Simple Grading System

Concepts used:
 input(),
 int()/float(),
 if-elif-else

Problem Statement
Write a Python program that:
1.Asks the user to enter their marks (out of 100).
2.Assigns a grade based on these rules:
   marks >= 90 → Grade A+
   80 <= marks < 90 → Grade A
   70 <= marks < 80 → Grade B
   60 <= marks < 70 → Grade C
   40 <= marks < 60 → Grade D
         marks < 40 → Fail


Prints the grade.
Also validate: if marks are < 0 or > 100, print an "Invalid marks" message instead of a grade.
Example Run

Enter your marks: 85
Grade: A

Enter your marks: 35
Grade: Fail

Enter your marks: 150
Invalid marks! Please enter a value between 0 and 100.

Bonus (optional)
1.Loop so the user can check multiple students until they type q to quit.
2.Track and print the average grade/marks of all students checked in that session (hint: keep a running total and a count).

